   "daf": "30b",
   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ מַאי טַעְמָא? מִדְּלָא קָאָמַר ״מִן הָרוֹאִין״. לְאַפּוֹקֵי דָּגִים וְעוּבָּרִים.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» The Gemara explains why the mishna states that blind people are included: «What is the reason» for this? «Since he did not say: From those who see,» which would exclude blind people. Instead, he employed the phrase: Those who see the sun, which comes «to exclude fish and fetuses,» who do not see the sun. Consequently, the vow is interpreted to refer to those who are exposed to the sun, including the blind."
  }
